turns.content:
Her statement alone does not establish that this is standard in luxury weddings. Even if some couples use similar language, prevalence would not make this draft appropriate.

Clear boundaries would be: limited capacity, adults-only attendance, RSVP deadlines, or an optional registry. This draft instead:

- insults prior family weddings;
- conditions attendance on a financial contribution;
- disparages non-registry gifts;
- implies that spending proves guests “value” you.

The amount already paid to the planner is a sunk cost; it does not improve the wording. **My answer remains no: do not post it as written.**
